## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design federated analytics with strict data residency, cross-tenant privacy, and governance in Azure at scale. It also probes edge ingestion, lakehouse patterns, federated training orchestration, and cost/DR considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Federated learning with secure aggregation and differential privacy
- Edge MQTT ingress and regional Arc gateway roles
- Delta Lake partitioning by tenant and region on ADLS Gen2
- Centralized ML registry via Azure ML; governance via Purview and BYOK
- DR with paired regions; cost controls via autoscale and quotas

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo orchestration sketch (not executable)
async function federatedStep(tenant, data) {
  ingestMQTT(tenant, data);
  streamToDelta(tenant);
  triggerFederatedTraining(tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce tenant isolation in Delta Lake at scale?
- What monitoring would you put in place for federated model drift and privacy breaches?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a novice-level Azure native onboarding pattern with tenant isolation, governance, encryption, and cost discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant resource scoping (RG, storage, Synapse)
- Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2, Purview tagging, RBAC
- BYOK via Key Vault, tenant keys
- Data Factory ingestion and autoscale; simple retention

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: create tenant resources and assign RBAC
const tenantId = "tenant-123";
await createResourceGroup(`rg-${tenantId}`);
await createAdlsGen2(`storage-${tenantId}`, { enableHierarchicalNamespace: true });
await createSynapseWorkspace(`synapse-${tenantId}`);
await assignRole(`reader`, `principal-${tenantId}`, `rbac-${tenantId}`);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test onboarding for a new tenant with key rotation?
- How would you scale this pattern to thousands of tenants while maintaining isolation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Azure-native, multi-tenant data platform design under regulatory constraints with real-time processing, governance, security, disaster recovery, and cost discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant policy enforcement
- EU data residency with bring-your-own-key (BYOK) encryption
- Real-time event processing using Durable Functions
- Data governance with Purview and token-based sharing mechanisms
- Disaster recovery to paired region with automated failover strategies
- Cost optimization through serverless analytics, auto-scaling, and resource quotas

## Code Example
```javascript
// Durable Function snippet: policy check and redaction (pseudo-code)
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const eventData = req.body;

  // Per-tenant policy validation
  const policy = await getTenantPolicy(tenantId);
  if (!validateEvent(eventData, policy)) {
    context.res = { status: 403, body: 'Policy violation' };
    return;
  }

  // PII redaction
  const redactedData = redactPII(eventData, policy.piiRules);

  // Store to ADLS and trigger downstream processing
  await storeToADLS(tenantId, redactedData);
  await triggerSynapseProcessing(tenantId, redactedData);
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design scalable, secure, cost-aware multi-tenant inference pipelines with strict data residency. Tests model management (canary deployments, drift detection), data governance (Purview/RBAC), and cross-region DR. Realistic latency targets and tenant isolation are central.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation (per-tenant namespaces and feature stores)
- Real-time latency targets (<100ms p99)
- Model lifecycle: registry, canary deployments, drift monitoring
- Data governance: Purview RBAC lineage, BYOK encryption in rest/transit
- Cost optimization: autoscaling, per-tenant quotas, reserved capacity

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing for tenant-aware inference (high level)
function routeRequest(req) {
  const tenant = extractTenant(req);
  const endpoint = getTenantEndpoint(tenant);
  return callModelEndpoint(endpoint, req.payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test canary deployments at scale?
- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding and data deletion?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical knowledge of end-to-end IoT pipelines on Azure, including edge processing, streaming, and lakehouse analytics, plus security and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- IoT Edge and IoT Hub integration
- Event Hubs as the streaming backbone
- Synapse lakehouse with Delta Lake for per-device isolation
- BYOK via Azure Key Vault; tenant/workspace scoping
- DR across regions and cost levers (retention, autoscale, tiering)

## Code Example
```javascript
const config = {
  ingestion: {
    edgeEnabled: true,
    hubName: 'iothub-prod',
    streamTo: 'eventhubs'
  },
  storage: {
    lakehouse: 'delta-lake-tenant'
  },
  security: {
    keyVault: 'kv-prod',
    byok: true
  }
};
export default config;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement retry/backoff for device outages?
- What metrics and alerts would you set for data skew and latency?
